# ---- Database ----------------------------------------------------------
# Leave unset to use the built-in local Postgres (PGlite) stored in .data/.
# Set for production: any Postgres, e.g. Neon or Supabase.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host/db?sslmode=require

# Demo data on a fresh database. Default: on in development, off in production.
# BRANDOS_SEED=on

# ---- Sign-in -----------------------------------------------------------
# "password": real accounts. Admins send invite links from the Team page.
#   This is the default in production (next build + next start).
# "demo": pick any teammate from a list, no passwords. Default in development.
# BRANDOS_AUTH=password

# Optional. With BRANDOS_SEED=off a fresh install shows a setup screen that
# creates the first admin, so these are only needed for scripted installs.
# The password is only applied if that account has none yet.
# BRANDOS_ADMIN_EMAIL=you@agency.com
# BRANDOS_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-to-something-long
# BRANDOS_ADMIN_NAME=Your Name

# Signs the short-lived cookies used half-way through a sign-in (the
# two-step code screen, the trip to Google). Needed when more than one
# server instance runs; without it each process makes up its own key.
# At least 16 characters. Make one with: openssl rand -hex 32
# AUTH_SECRET=

# ---- Sign in with Google (optional) -----------------------------------
# Shows "Continue with Google" on the sign-in page (password mode only).
# Google never creates accounts: the Google email must already belong to
# someone on the Team page. Invited people can join this way without
# setting a password. Create an OAuth client ("Web application") at
# console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials, and add the
# redirect URI  APP_URL + /api/auth/google/callback
# e.g. https://brandos.youragency.com/api/auth/google/callback
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Only let addresses at this domain sign in with Google.
# GOOGLE_ALLOWED_DOMAIN=youragency.com

# ---- Files -------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave unset to keep uploads in .data/uploads. On Vercel, connect a Blob
# store; files are stored private and served only to people who can see them.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# Largest file people can upload to an asset, in MB. Default: 25.
# MAX_UPLOAD_MB=25

# ---- Email --------------------------------------------------------------
# Invites, password resets, review requests, requested changes, approvals
# and @mentions are emailed when this is set (free account at resend.com).
# Each person picks instant / daily digest / off in Settings → Notifications.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# Sender, once your domain is verified in Resend. Until then Resend's test
# sender only delivers to the address you signed up with.
# MAIL_FROM=BrandOS <brandos@youragency.com>
# The public address of this install, used for links inside emails, Slack
# posts and calendar feeds.
# APP_URL=https://brandos.youragency.com

# ---- Daily digest ------------------------------------------------------
# Turns on the morning digest and due-date reminders. Something must call
# /api/cron/digest once a day with the header
#   Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET
# (docs/DEPLOY.md shows the Coolify scheduled task). Without it, anything set
# to "Daily digest" is emailed straight away instead. The digest goes out at
# most once per person per day, in the server's time zone (set TZ to change).
# Make one with: openssl rand -hex 32
# CRON_SECRET=

# ---- Slack -------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. A Slack incoming webhook for one channel (api.slack.com/messaging/webhooks).
# Review requests, approvals, change requests and new client links are posted
# there with a link to the work. Admins can send a test from Settings.
# SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/...

# ---- AI drafting -------------------------------------------------------
# Enables "Draft with AI" on assets (Claude writes copy in the brand's voice).
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# ---- Security ----------------------------------------------------------
# New passwords are checked against Have I Been Pwned's range API (only the
# first five characters of a SHA-1 hash leave the server). If the service
# does not answer within 3 s the password is allowed and a warning is logged.
# Set to "off" to skip the check, e.g. on an install with no internet access.
# PWNED_CHECK=off

# ---- Operations --------------------------------------------------------
# The commit being run, shown as "version" by /api/health. The Docker image
# sets it from its GIT_SHA build argument; without it the package version shows.
# GIT_SHA=
